// A bogus method on a concrete numeric receiver is caught statically by
// HARN-NAM-005: `float` exposes no `frobnicate`, so the mistake is a
// compile-time type error rather than a silent `nil` or a deferred runtime
// throw. (The VM keeps a runtime throw as defense-in-depth for receivers
// whose type escapes static analysis — see `call_number_method`.)
pipeline default() {
  const _ = 3.14.frobnicate()
}
